pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.0.3-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add --no-rbd flag / DISABLE_RBD config option to build pve-qemu-kvm
    without RBD/Ceph support: drops librbd-dev from Build-Depends and
    flips --enable-rbd to --disable-rbd in debian/rules. Needed when the
    PVE Ceph repo hasn't published librbd-dev/librados-dev matching the
    currently-installed librbd1/librados2 point release (a recurring
    situation right after a Ceph hotfix), since forcing that version
    match otherwise makes apt want to remove ceph-common and everything
    depending on it (pve-manager, qemu-server, pve-ha-manager,
    pve-container, proxmox-ve) to reconcile versions

 -- Hikaru <i@rua.moe>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800

pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.0.2-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add QEMU 11.0 support for pve-qemu-kvm 11.0.0-3 (Proxmox VE 9.2.2)
  * Fix hw/pci-host/gpex.c hunk: context line removed upstream
    (set_bit(DEVICE_CATEGORY_BRIDGE, ...) no longer precedes dc->desc)
  * Fix hw/scsi/scsi-bus.c hunk: qemu_hw_version() call replaced with
    QEMU_HW_VERSION macro upstream
  * Fix hw/smbios/smbios.c hunk: SMBIOS VM flag logic was refactored
    upstream into a conditional `if (smbios_type0.vm)` block; the
    anti-detection patch now neutralizes that block directly instead of
    hardcoding the old combined 0x14->0x08 byte value, which no longer
    matches the new code structure
  * Sync patches/001-anti-detection.patch with 001-anti-detection.patch;
    the shipped copy had drifted and still contained the KVM CPUID
    signature hunk that was reverted from the root copy in 1.0.1

 -- Hikaru <i@rua.moe>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800

pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.0.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add --cn/--china flag for China mainland mirror mode (GitHub mirrors)
  * Add USE_CN_MIRROR config option for persistent mirror setting
  * Fix KVM CPUID signature: remove kvm.c patch to preserve Linux VM
    paravirtualization (kvm-clock, PV EOI, PV spinlocks, PV IPIs)
  * Update documentation with China mirror instructions and KVM/Windows
    VM configuration guidance

 -- Hikaru <i@rua.moe>  Mon, 21 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0800

pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.0.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release
  * DKMS-like auto-patching mechanism for pve-qemu-kvm
  * APT hook integration for automatic rebuild on upgrade
  * systemd service for background rebuilds
  * CLI tool for manual management

